An alternative to clockwork that might be simpler to program would be to
make the automaton steam powered, with various quality lumps of coal
taking the place of normal food, monsters still inedible, and refilling
the water tank at a fountain, pool, moat or sink needed on a regular
basis. Since fountains and sinks go away after a while, this would put
some time pressure on the automaton to finish the game quickly. Sokoban
and Mines would be time trials, being dry, or perhaps potions of water
would be usable as refill backups but supply no other benefit.

Since much of the game paraphenalia would be useless to an automaton as
described, might as well give it a huge carrying capacity; it won't help
much, but might afford a new style of play for this one race.

It would be unlikely to be able to #jump, we sort of see it as more of a
lurcher than a ballet star.

Only a warhorse would work for a saddle beast, and even that should be
slowed significantly when ridden.

